      "detail": "8th in Atlantic Division",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The season didn't drift to a close so much as <strong>collapse into the long dark</strong> - 78 points, a 32-36-14 record, dead last in the Atlantic at 8th, and a minus-31 margin in the standings that says more about the mess than any speech ever could. <strong>Seven straight losses ended a year that never found a spine</strong>, and the front office now has to decide whether this was a one-year skid or the natural bill coming due for too many soft edges and too few answers. The goaltending was part of the problem, with Joseph Woll grinding through a 15-16-7 season and a 3.34 goals-against average, a line that matches the mood of the room: overworked, undercut, and asked to stand in front of too much traffic. Now comes the hard part - coaching questions, roster churn, and free agency decisions that will test whether this club can stop pretending it is only one tweak away from respectability. <strong>The next chapter is about accountability, not excuses, and the first real clue will be who is still standing behind the bench when camp opens</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated May 27, 2026"
      },
