        "body": "The draft board has finally stopped spinning, and now the Washington operation is living with its choices - the rookies, the fits and the bets that could change a depth chart before camp even opens. <strong>Josh Conerly Jr. and the rest of the class are the real story now</strong>, because this roster sits 3rd in the NFC East, 6 games back, with a 1-game winning streak and a 14th-place playoff seed that only underlines how much work remains. The Commanders needed help in the trenches and on the perimeter, and the question is not whether the front office added bodies but whether it added immediate answers. Conerly gives them athletic upside at tackle, while the rest of the rookie group has to prove it can handle NFL pace, protection calls and the uglier chores of this scheme. That is where April becomes June in a hurry. The best clubs turn draft weekend into a lineup issue by training camp; the rest merely collect names. <strong>What matters next is whether the rookies can force their way into meaningful snaps before the veterans lock the room shut</strong>.",
